WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Argentina is the second-largest nation in South America, spanning from the subtropics to Tierra del Fuego.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
In Mendoza province, Mount Aconcagua towers at 6,961 meters as the highest peak in the Americas.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
Los Glaciares National Park showcases the thunderous Perito Moreno Glacier in Santa Cruz.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Across the Pampas plains, traditional Gaucho horsemen wear wool ponchos and silver rastra belts.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Buenos Aires is the birthplace of Tango, accompanied by the resonant 71-button acoustic Bandoneón.

